                  <msItem>
                     <title>W. Woodford etc.</title>
                     <note type="MLGB3_generalNotes">Two discrete manuscripts bound together: the
                        first is larger than the second. Medieval binding of white leather over
                        boards, with chemise. Strap and pin fastening. Label on upper part of lower
                        cover of chemise, and at the foot part of the metal of the chain attachment,
                        secured by four nals. The label is inscribed 'Continentur in hoc libro
                        conclusiones Willelmi Wyford' contra conclusiones Wykelyff. Item defensorium
                        donacionis ecclesie Magistri Ricardi Ullerston' doctoris in theologia
                        Oxon''. This is covered by horn fastened with six nails. The chain
                        attachment is of the same pattern as the perfect one on Exeter 3512, but
                        here it has been cut off at the point where it would have projected below
                        the bottom of the book.</note>
                  </msItem>
               </msContents>
               <history>
                  <origin>
                     <origDate when-custom="14XX">s. xv</origDate>
                  </origin>
                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_1">Exeter, Devon. Cathedral
                        church of St Peter. </orgName><p>At end of the first item is 'Liber M'
                        henrici Webber decani ecclesie Cath' Exon'', and, on verso of front flyleaf,
                        'Hunc librum disposuit magister Henricus Webber Decanus Ecclesie Cathedralis
                        Exon' Magne librarie Ecclesie Cath' predict' de bonis suis propriis'.
                        </p><note type="MLGB3_medievalCatalogueNotes">Cat. p. 370;
                     Leland</note></provenance>
               </history>
